      "description": "This deliberately grouped SysCoI resource covers two linked works by Gabriel Burstein and Constantin Virgil Negoita. The 2011 Kybernetes paper proposes a Kabbalah Tree of Life-based cybernetic framework for cognition, emotion, and action using feedback, hierarchical control, multi-valued logic, and category theory. Their 2014 chapter develops the proposal for knowledge-based behavioural economics and finance, drawing on system dynamics, emotional intelligence, and tacit knowledge. These are the authors' theoretical propositions, not independent proof that the framework explains or resolves societal problems.",
